      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Michael, good catch. Thanks for reporting it.\n\nThis is a real bug, with `__adjust_next_start()` we expand next backwards, subtraction in `linear_page_index(next, vmg-\u003eend)` underflows, leaving next-\u003evm_pgoff garbage (hence the SIGBUS past EOF) as you found.\n\nFixed in latest verions by deriving the `pgoff` (and slice offset) from `vmg-\u003emiddle`, which always contains `vmg-\u003eend`. Verified with your reproducer.",
